<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar outflows at $26.7 mln Oct 24.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar outflows at $26.7 mln Oct 24.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $26.7 million deficit on October 24 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON OCTOBER 24</p>
<p>Exports: $144.1 million</p>
<p>Imports: $220.6 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $308.1 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $258.3 million</p>
<p>Deficit: $26.7 million</p>
<p>OCTOBER DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $2.932 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $3.173 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $5.247 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $3.322 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $1.684 billion</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2324411</p>
</text>
